### `kernel/src/graph_capture.cu` (ticket 10, kernel-abi-03, GitHub #10)
Eager CUDA-graph capture at startup (design §1/§2): the `extern "C"`
functions `ignis_graph_begin_capture`, `ignis_graph_end_capture`,
`ignis_graph_launch`, `ignis_graph_destroy` (the flat C ABI capture
surface — an opaque `struct ignis_graph` handle owning the captured graph,
its instantiated executable, and, when the leaf created the capture
stream, the stream itself) plus `ignis_graph_startup_check` (the startup
verification: capture a representative prefill + decode kernel sequence —
the ticket-05 GQA prefill attention + GDN step and the ticket-03 GQA
decode attention, a few KB of VRAM — into a CUDA graph, replay it, and
confirm the replayed outputs match the eager outputs bit-exactly; the
99% performance gate on the canary suite is ADR 0007 / ignis-bench,
ticket 20). Built on the CUDA runtime stream-capture API
(`cudaStreamBeginCapture` / `cudaStreamEndCapture` /
`cudaGraphInstantiate` / `cudaGraphLaunch`); the captured launches are
the ported kernels from the sibling .cuh files, launched directly with
`<<<>>>` on the capture stream (the host-pointer surfaces do their H2D/
D2H on the legacy stream, which cannot be captured — the v1 serving loop
keeps activations device-resident, so the graph holds only kernel nodes).
The launch configurations mirror the ticket-05/03 surfaces 1:1. There is
no reference equivalent (the reference's driver was the engine's op
dispatch, and its graph capture was engine-internals C++ state the flat C
ABI of ADR 0001 forbids across the boundary); this is new C ABI surface
for the v1 eager-graph decision (self-contained; provenance in
kernel/NOTICE, as with the sibling surfaces).

### `kernel/src/nvfp4_gemm_prefill.cuh` (ticket 22, kernel-abi-05, GitHub #22)
Multi-token NVFP4 GEMM (the prefill / FFN-projection path). Adapted from the
reference bf16-activation small-tokens NVFP4 GEMM
(`ops/linear/nvfp4/nvfp4_small_t.cuh` — the rowsplit "rows-of-W × tokens"
tiling with fp32 FMA accumulation, bf16 activations × dequantized NVFP4
weights) and its large-tokens rowsplit grid structure
(`nvfp4_w4a4_mma.cuh`: grid.x over m-rows, grid.y over token tiles). The
reference kernels are driven by the engine's Geometry/Schedule/RowPolicy/
Epilogue dispatch and use Programmatic Dependent Launch (PDL); the
large-tokens path is a tensor-core W4A4 MMA that requires FP4-quantized
*activations*. That dispatch layer is C++ state, which the flat C ABI of
ADR 0001 forbids across the boundary, so it is not ported; the PDL syncs are
stripped in favor of plain `<<<>>>` launches; and the tensor-core W4A4 MMA
(which needs FP4 activations, not the bf16 activations of this ABI) is
deferred to the performance gate (ADR 0007). The math (bf16 activations ×
E2M1/E4M3-dequantized NVFP4 weights, fp32 FMA accumulation, the rowsplit
grid, and the plain row-major [m][k/2] / [m][k/16] code/scale layouts) is
ported 1:1; the E2M1/E4M3 decode helpers are ported 1:1 (inlined in the header
with a `gemm_prefill_` prefix, to keep it self-contained and avoid pulling the
ticket-03 GEMV kernel into this translation unit), so a `tokens == 1` call
matches the single-token GEMV. Self-contained; compiles standalone in the leaf.

