### `kernel/src/gdn_causal_conv.cuh` (ticket 28, kernel-abi 06, GitHub #28)
GDN 4-tap depthwise causal conv + SiLU (the `gdn/convolution` tensor).
Adapted from the reference GDN projected-input conv
(`ops/gdn_input_proj/gdn_projected_conv.cu`: `gdn_projected_conv_kernel` —
one thread per channel; the rolling 3-tap state s0,s1,s2 + the current tap
p; the 4-tap fma chain `w0*s0 + w1*s1 + w2*s2 + w3*p`; the SiLU epilogue
`x / (1 + exp(-x))` from `ops/common/math.cuh`). The reference kernel is a
per-(channel, batch) machine driven by the engine's Tensor dispatch
(separate query/key/value output tensors, a per-batch valid-column count,
a slot-indexed state pool, and the `Publish` snapshot/record templates).
That dispatch layer is C++ state, which the flat C ABI of ADR 0001 forbids
across the boundary, so it is not ported; the per-channel rolling conv math
(the fma chain, the SiLU, the 3-tap state shift) is ported 1:1 to the flat
C ABI geometry (the single-sequence [tokens][channels] projection, the
per-channel state [channels][3], the single `out` buffer — the `z` rows are
not part of `channels`, they bypass the conv entirely). Self-contained;
compiles standalone in the leaf.

### `kernel/src/rope_qk.cuh` (ticket 28, kernel-abi 06, GitHub #28)
GQA split-half NeoX RoPE (in-place on Q and K). Adapted from the reference
rope (`ops/kernel/rope.cuh`: `apply_rope_head` — the split-half pair
rotation `out[p] = a*cos − b*sin`, `out[p + R/2] = b*cos + a·s`, with the
per-block shared cos/sin cache — the fixed-sincos pattern — and the legacy
unscaled route: the fp32 product + `sincosf`, the bit-stable engine
history, `attention_factor` 1.0), plus its inv_freq table
(`ops/wrapper/rope.cpp`: `rope_linear_frequencies`,
`inv_freq[p] = θ^(-2p/rotary_dim)`; the table is computed once at
construction, host-side, a deterministic table — the Rust builder
`rope_inv_frequencies` in `crates/core/src/compute.rs`, passed to the
kernel as the f32 `inv_freq` argument). The reference fuses
rope(rmsnorm(x)) (`ops/launcher/qk_norm_rope.cu`); the v1 does the
`ignis_rmsnorm` (kernel-abi 02) + this RoPE as two steps (the fused kernel
is the later performance item, ADR 0005). The reference's RopeKernelMode /
QHeads / KHeads template dispatch, the PDL syncs, and the attention-factor
(YaRN) scaling are not ported (C++ state the flat C ABI of ADR 0001
forbids; v1 is unscaled, factor 1.0 — the attention-factor scaling is a
later performance item, ADR 0005); the pair-rotation math is ported 1:1.
Self-contained; compiles standalone in the leaf.

